1
00:01:30,530 --> 00:01:34,979
[AWAKEN]

2
00:01:35,640 --> 00:01:37,930
[Episode 4]

3
00:01:42,070 --> 00:01:42,870
Inspector Su,

4
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:44,180
any instructions?

5
00:01:44,350 --> 00:01:46,200
I'll speak to
Director Li personally tomorrow.

6
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:47,259
That would be best.

7
00:02:04,790 --> 00:02:05,480
Hello.

8
00:02:05,760 --> 00:02:06,840
Director, it's me.

9
00:02:08,030 --> 00:02:09,430
Do you have any idea what time it is?

10
00:02:09,430 --> 00:02:11,090
Can't it wait until tomorrow?

11
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:14,190
Su Men suddenly decided to
interrogate that Chen guy.

12
00:02:14,190 --> 00:02:15,430
I don't know what she asked him.

13
00:02:15,430 --> 00:02:17,829
She said she'd
tell you in person tomorrow.

14
00:02:18,520 --> 00:02:20,190
This woman is such a nuisance.

15
00:02:21,090 --> 00:02:22,420
Doesn't she ever sleep?

16
00:02:26,120 --> 00:02:27,710
Is the confession ready?

17
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:30,050
Yes. All the paperwork is in order.

18
00:02:30,510 --> 00:02:32,630
Have him executed along with
tomorrow morning's first batch.

19
00:02:32,630 --> 00:02:34,400
Once it's taken care of, I'll go see her.

20
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:35,710
Better not leave room for complications.

21
00:02:35,710 --> 00:02:36,440
Understood.

22
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:14,310
For you.

23
00:03:15,630 --> 00:03:16,490
Flowers again?

24
00:03:17,360 --> 00:03:18,760
Aren't you tired of this?

25
00:03:18,840 --> 00:03:19,840
Please take them.

26
00:03:34,150 --> 00:03:35,950
Do you happen to have 5,000 yuan?

27
00:03:36,400 --> 00:03:37,120
I do.

28
00:03:37,590 --> 00:03:38,240
Good.

29
00:03:38,590 --> 00:03:40,320
Then drive me to the Paramount.

30
00:03:40,430 --> 00:03:41,520
The Paramount?

31
00:03:50,440 --> 00:03:53,079
[In January 1942, I borrowed 5,000 yuan
from Young Master Feng—Jinbao]

32
00:03:54,280 --> 00:03:56,370
Actually, you don't need to
write me an IOU.

33
00:03:56,370 --> 00:03:58,500
It's not that I can't spare 5,000 yuan.

34
00:03:59,430 --> 00:04:00,760
You giving it to me is one thing—

35
00:04:00,760 --> 00:04:02,760
my borrowing it from you is another.

36
00:04:02,870 --> 00:04:05,280
Even close brothers
should keep accounts straight.

37
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:07,630
Could you come to
Chongqing with me and settle down?

38
00:04:07,630 --> 00:04:09,520
We could open a small match factory

39
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:10,780
and live a simple life.

40
00:04:15,910 --> 00:04:18,370
Who says I want to
live a simple life with you?

41
00:04:18,940 --> 00:04:20,940
Chongqing? I've never been there.

42
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,330
Is it as big as Shanghai?

43
00:04:31,870 --> 00:04:33,000
You're Shasha?

44
00:04:33,630 --> 00:04:34,480
I'm Jinbao.

45
00:04:35,360 --> 00:04:37,159
Give the flowers to Miss Shasha.

46
00:04:37,659 --> 00:04:40,440
[Shasha, Dance Hall Girl]

47
00:04:39,030 --> 00:04:40,760
What kind of character are you?

48
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:42,040
He's no "character."

49
00:04:42,040 --> 00:04:43,240
He's Young Master Feng.

50
00:04:43,240 --> 00:04:45,240
I stole him from Bingbing.

51
00:04:47,310 --> 00:04:48,510
Like Bingbing,

52
00:04:48,580 --> 00:04:49,750
I'm also with MGM.

53
00:04:56,600 --> 00:04:57,950
You should've seen the look

54
00:04:57,950 --> 00:04:59,600
on Bingbing's face that day.

55
00:05:00,050 --> 00:05:01,070
Her expression

56
00:05:01,120 --> 00:05:03,000
was as sour as spoiled soup.

57
00:05:09,070 --> 00:05:11,120
That bitch finally got
what was coming to her.

58
00:05:11,120 --> 00:05:12,970
Back when I worked at MGM,

59
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:14,460
she gave me no end of grief.

60
00:05:14,750 --> 00:05:16,480
We're both women fallen on hard times.

61
00:05:16,480 --> 00:05:17,920
I'm sure we'll become good sisters.

62
00:05:17,920 --> 00:05:20,120
Come on. I'll buy you a late-night meal.

63
00:05:22,940 --> 00:05:24,180
I, Zhu Dahei,

64
00:05:24,210 --> 00:05:26,410
hereby become
sworn sisters with you, Jinbao.

65
00:05:26,410 --> 00:05:28,190
We may not be born on the same day,

66
00:05:28,190 --> 00:05:30,070
but we shall die on the same day.

67
00:05:30,270 --> 00:05:31,270
Die? No way.

68
00:05:31,390 --> 00:05:33,120
I want us both to live forever—

69
00:05:33,240 --> 00:05:34,240
let's be fairies.

70
00:05:35,310 --> 00:05:35,950
Okay.

71
00:05:44,920 --> 00:05:46,480
Flowers—for the fairy.

72
00:05:46,780 --> 00:05:48,580
Money—for Captain Cang.

73
00:05:55,240 --> 00:05:56,840
You have a friend in trouble?

74
00:05:59,820 --> 00:06:00,900
It's my lover.

75
00:06:04,090 --> 00:06:04,760
Drink.

76
00:06:06,560 --> 00:06:07,160
Alright.

77
00:06:35,020 --> 00:06:36,020
Inspector Su.

78
00:06:37,270 --> 00:06:38,159
Captain Cang.

79
00:06:39,310 --> 00:06:40,800
In such a rush to execute him?

80
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:42,600
I'm just carrying out my duties.

81
00:06:42,680 --> 00:06:43,940
Who gave you the order?

82
00:06:48,920 --> 00:06:51,040
I'm acting according to regulations.

83
00:06:51,040 --> 00:06:52,370
Here is his confession.

84
00:07:01,830 --> 00:07:04,090
I'm the inspector overseeing this case.

85
00:07:04,390 --> 00:07:05,590
Without my approval,

86
00:07:06,120 --> 00:07:07,560
no one shall execute him.

87
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:21,720
An outsider with no background at all

88
00:07:21,720 --> 00:07:24,180
is actually the one
who killed Yu Yingxiang?

89
00:07:24,600 --> 00:07:25,390
Director Li,

90
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:27,730
do you accept that conclusion?

91
00:07:31,510 --> 00:07:32,970
But he's the only suspect.

92
00:07:39,240 --> 00:07:41,640
The motive for the murder
was simply money.

93
00:07:45,270 --> 00:07:48,120
Yu Yingxiang's collusion with the NBIS
is a major case.

94
00:07:48,120 --> 00:07:49,070
Yet you're putting on

95
00:07:49,070 --> 00:07:51,870
this coerced-confession act
right in front of me?

96
00:07:51,920 --> 00:07:54,000
Even if Yu Yingxiang had been captured,

97
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:55,560
he'd have been executed anyway.

98
00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:57,750
At least he got an easy death.

99
00:07:58,720 --> 00:07:59,750
This case

100
00:07:59,750 --> 00:08:01,560
has to be brought to an end eventually.

101
00:08:01,560 --> 00:08:04,420
The Japanese are
still waiting for an explanation.

102
00:08:05,170 --> 00:08:06,700
The Japanese aren't fools.

103
00:08:07,380 --> 00:08:08,980
If you hand them this result,

104
00:08:09,630 --> 00:08:12,160
they'll only think
you're brushing them off.

105
00:08:13,120 --> 00:08:14,380
Then, in your opinion,

106
00:08:15,310 --> 00:08:17,240
if that guy is not the one who did it,

107
00:08:17,310 --> 00:08:18,800
how did Yu Yingxiang die?

108
00:08:21,390 --> 00:08:22,390
Could he have

109
00:08:22,830 --> 00:08:25,160
committed suicide to escape punishment?

110
00:08:31,600 --> 00:08:32,360
Suicide?

111
00:08:36,909 --> 00:08:38,710
Suicide would actually hold up.

112
00:08:43,150 --> 00:08:43,960
Understood.

113
00:08:46,080 --> 00:08:47,910
Then, what about that guy?

114
00:08:49,440 --> 00:08:51,440
That guy has nothing to do with this.

115
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:53,330
You and I both know that.

116
00:08:56,150 --> 00:08:56,750
Alright.

117
00:08:58,040 --> 00:09:00,240
Then we will do as you say, Inspector Su.

118
00:09:01,510 --> 00:09:03,950
He committed suicide to escape punishment.

119
00:09:03,950 --> 00:09:05,550
That accounts for his death.

120
00:09:07,120 --> 00:09:08,840
What about the money he embezzled?

121
00:09:08,840 --> 00:09:10,040
Please rest assured.

122
00:09:10,480 --> 00:09:13,270
I'll recover every penny of the money

123
00:09:13,560 --> 00:09:14,910
Yu Yingxiang embezzled,

124
00:09:14,910 --> 00:09:17,310
so you'll have something proper to report.

125
00:09:20,630 --> 00:09:22,720
I've heard you like green tea.

126
00:09:23,370 --> 00:09:25,620
I've prepared some especially for you.

127
00:09:34,480 --> 00:09:36,000
Newspapers! Get your newspapers!

128
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:37,930
Newspapers! Get your newspapers!

129
00:09:40,340 --> 00:09:42,870
Yu Yingxiang's case
is closed just like that?

130
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,600
Yu Yingxiang must've

131
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:47,800
acted alone in colluding with the NBIS.

132
00:09:48,840 --> 00:09:50,650
Li Moqun had him eliminated

133
00:09:50,680 --> 00:09:52,210
to cover up the corruption.

134
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:55,140
We'll never find that killer.

135
00:09:56,030 --> 00:09:59,030
And even if we did,
we wouldn't get anything out of him.

136
00:09:59,750 --> 00:10:03,010
There's no need to
make Chen Kailai the scapegoat for this.

137
00:10:03,510 --> 00:10:05,870
Chen Kailai is quite unlucky.

138
00:10:08,600 --> 00:10:09,750
How did he manage to survive

139
00:10:09,750 --> 00:10:11,960
the interrogation at No. 76?

140
00:10:16,230 --> 00:10:17,830
Can you release Chen Kailai?

141
00:10:18,400 --> 00:10:19,930
He's an innocent civilian.

142
00:10:20,720 --> 00:10:21,790
I've been busy all night.

143
00:10:21,790 --> 00:10:23,480
I just wanted to get some good sleep.

144
00:10:23,480 --> 00:10:25,340
Let's talk about it another time.

145
00:10:25,870 --> 00:10:27,270
Important matters

146
00:10:27,440 --> 00:10:29,640
should be raised at the important time.

147
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:30,870
Besides,

148
00:10:31,160 --> 00:10:33,910
you came back to sleep,
and yet you still want to do this?

149
00:10:33,910 --> 00:10:35,720
I just wanted to sleep better.

150
00:10:38,270 --> 00:10:39,840
I already promised my sworn sister

151
00:10:39,840 --> 00:10:41,100
I'd intercede for him.

152
00:10:45,080 --> 00:10:46,870
None of you women are any good!

153
00:10:51,240 --> 00:10:52,840
Chen Kailai cannot be released.

154
00:10:52,840 --> 00:10:53,790
That's an order.

155
00:10:55,670 --> 00:10:57,400
I've already taken the money.

156
00:10:57,780 --> 00:10:58,880
Think of something.

157
00:10:58,880 --> 00:11:00,080
Then give the money back!

158
00:11:00,080 --> 00:11:01,010
I'm telling you,

159
00:11:01,870 --> 00:11:03,630
no one can save Chen Kailai.

160
00:11:05,550 --> 00:11:08,790
How come you were able to release
all those other people before?

161
00:11:08,790 --> 00:11:10,510
Useless thing.

162
00:11:10,510 --> 00:11:12,440
All you ever do is crawl into my bed.

163
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:21,790
Hello?

164
00:11:22,010 --> 00:11:23,270
Come back immediately

165
00:11:23,550 --> 00:11:24,950
and release Chen Kailai.

166
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:27,600
Yes.

167
00:11:34,750 --> 00:11:37,350
She's my best sworn sister.

168
00:11:56,290 --> 00:11:57,750
Alright, alright.

169
00:11:58,550 --> 00:11:59,950
There, there. Don't cry.

170
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:04,800
Let me ask you.

171
00:12:05,910 --> 00:12:07,280
How much did your sworn sister

172
00:12:07,280 --> 00:12:08,070
give you?

173
00:12:11,670 --> 00:12:12,550
Four thousand.

174
00:12:16,120 --> 00:12:17,670
Four thousand's a bit low.

175
00:12:21,120 --> 00:12:22,380
Let me see what I can do.

176
00:12:25,150 --> 00:12:26,000
Cang,

177
00:12:26,270 --> 00:12:27,670
you really are a good man.

178
00:12:47,550 --> 00:12:49,200
The latest German model.

179
00:12:53,550 --> 00:12:55,100
It's a waste in my hands.

180
00:13:02,510 --> 00:13:04,370
Could you take a photograph of me?

181
00:13:11,550 --> 00:13:12,440
Here's fine.

182
00:13:16,870 --> 00:13:17,390
Okay.

183
00:13:43,790 --> 00:13:45,590
"Justice for all under heaven."

184
00:13:50,220 --> 00:13:51,680
Is there any justice here?

185
00:13:59,150 --> 00:14:00,610
Let me take you home first.

186
00:14:33,510 --> 00:14:34,320
I know.

187
00:14:35,240 --> 00:14:37,550
If it weren't for her,
I wouldn't be out today.

188
00:14:37,550 --> 00:14:39,390
It's hard to survive in Shanghai.

189
00:14:39,390 --> 00:14:41,050
Connections are everything.

190
00:15:20,970 --> 00:15:23,570
You really don't know
who killed Yu Yingxiang?

191
00:15:32,790 --> 00:15:33,440
General,

192
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:37,080
why do you think
Yu Yingxiang wanted so much money?

193
00:15:37,960 --> 00:15:39,090
A man only needs food

194
00:15:39,320 --> 00:15:41,320
and a roof over his head in this life.

195
00:15:41,720 --> 00:15:44,510
All that money—you can't take it along
when you die, nor spend it all while alive.

196
00:15:44,510 --> 00:15:46,960
And in the end, he died by his own hand.

197
00:15:53,390 --> 00:15:55,000
Money is still necessary.

198
00:15:57,150 --> 00:15:59,360
But greed, anger, and ignorance

199
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:02,600
are the great taboos of life.

200
00:16:03,390 --> 00:16:04,650
And greed is the worst.

201
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:17,910
Director Li,

202
00:16:19,120 --> 00:16:21,750
this matter was handled a bit hastily.

203
00:16:23,510 --> 00:16:24,390
Yes, General.

204
00:16:25,030 --> 00:16:26,000
We did

205
00:16:26,510 --> 00:16:28,960
handle this matter rather hastily.

206
00:16:33,750 --> 00:16:36,360
And regarding Yu Yingxiang's leaking
of information

207
00:16:36,360 --> 00:16:38,030
that got Mr. Suzuki killed in Hangzhou,

208
00:16:38,030 --> 00:16:39,830
and his collusion with the NBIS—

209
00:16:41,360 --> 00:16:43,820
shouldn't we investigate that thoroughly?

210
00:16:45,600 --> 00:16:47,260
Since the man is already dead,

211
00:16:47,670 --> 00:16:49,530
the matter can only stand as it is.

212
00:16:50,360 --> 00:16:52,750
I just wonder
whether he had any accomplices

213
00:16:52,750 --> 00:16:54,030
within No. 76.

214
00:16:54,960 --> 00:16:57,160
This is a serious threat to Director Li.

215
00:16:58,960 --> 00:17:00,560
It's also kept me up at night.

216
00:17:11,790 --> 00:17:13,960
Make a few extra dishes tonight.

217
00:17:15,190 --> 00:17:16,390
Yangzhou fried rice,

218
00:17:16,680 --> 00:17:18,200
stir-fried shredded pork
with winter bamboo shoots,

219
00:17:18,200 --> 00:17:20,800
and stir-fried cabbage
with water chestnuts!

220
00:17:21,240 --> 00:17:23,170
Every blind man can tell fortunes.

221
00:17:23,680 --> 00:17:26,510
Tonight we're welcoming my disciple back!

222
00:17:40,550 --> 00:17:42,510
We still need to make fried tofu puffs.

223
00:17:42,510 --> 00:17:43,920
Aside from Yangzhou fried rice,

224
00:17:43,920 --> 00:17:45,240
they're his favorite.

225
00:17:47,310 --> 00:17:57,480
♪ A true gentleman
never forgets a kindness ♪

226
00:18:01,590 --> 00:18:02,270
Thank you.

227
00:18:02,270 --> 00:18:03,200
You're welcome.

228
00:18:06,480 --> 00:18:09,200
♪ Ungrateful ♪

229
00:18:10,270 --> 00:18:12,400
The agency has received intelligence

230
00:18:13,030 --> 00:18:15,350
that the Communist operative
code-named Diana

231
00:18:15,350 --> 00:18:16,810
has begun to make her move.

232
00:18:17,880 --> 00:18:20,160
The NBIS's agent God of Wealth
has also been activated

233
00:18:20,160 --> 00:18:21,760
and has arrived in Shanghai.

234
00:18:22,550 --> 00:18:24,400
They must all be related

235
00:18:24,400 --> 00:18:26,240
to our Project Slumber.

236
00:18:27,880 --> 00:18:32,240
No. 76 is the security bureau
Mr. Wang trusts.

237
00:18:33,680 --> 00:18:34,920
You mustn't let

238
00:18:35,680 --> 00:18:37,810
what happened to Suzuki happen again.

239
00:18:38,440 --> 00:18:39,030
Yes.

240
00:18:40,680 --> 00:18:42,200
Why is Shanghai

241
00:18:42,200 --> 00:18:43,680
crawling with spies?

242
00:18:45,350 --> 00:18:46,720
Director Li, you've been
racking your brain over this.

243
00:18:46,720 --> 00:18:48,580
You must be feeling overwhelmed.

244
00:18:48,680 --> 00:18:49,790
You're not even that old,

245
00:18:49,790 --> 00:18:51,520
but you already have gray hair.

246
00:18:52,440 --> 00:18:56,100
Now corruption and collusion with the NBIS
are tangled together.

247
00:18:56,830 --> 00:18:57,550
General,

248
00:18:58,270 --> 00:19:00,200
I should've taken up a post at No. 76

249
00:19:00,510 --> 00:19:02,770
and started the investigation long ago.

250
00:19:04,920 --> 00:19:05,650
Director Li,

251
00:19:06,750 --> 00:19:08,110
I assume you have no objection

252
00:19:08,110 --> 00:19:10,960
to my helping you
root out the internal threats, right?

253
00:19:10,960 --> 00:19:11,760
Inspector Su,

254
00:19:12,480 --> 00:19:13,810
of course I support you.

255
00:19:13,840 --> 00:19:15,030
It's just that it's too chaotic

256
00:19:15,030 --> 00:19:17,030
and dangerous at No. 76.

257
00:19:18,640 --> 00:19:20,510
I was targeted for assassination
as soon as I got off the train.

258
00:19:20,510 --> 00:19:22,840
They meant to stop me from investigating.

259
00:19:22,920 --> 00:19:23,720
Could No. 76

260
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:25,260
be any more dangerous?

261
00:19:29,880 --> 00:19:33,270
I still have faith in
your abilities, Director Li.

262
00:19:35,310 --> 00:19:38,790
But now is a critical moment
for purging the traitors.

263
00:19:41,190 --> 00:19:44,460
Inspector Su, I hope you'll
take up a post at No. 76

264
00:19:45,070 --> 00:19:49,160
and assist Director Li in
carrying out this operation.

265
00:19:50,960 --> 00:19:52,830
Thank you for your trust, General.

266
00:19:52,830 --> 00:19:53,640
I agree.

267
00:19:54,750 --> 00:19:55,350
Good.

268
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:59,750
I hope you two can work together

269
00:20:00,470 --> 00:20:03,840
and ensure Project Slumber
proceeds smoothly.

270
00:20:07,310 --> 00:20:09,070
Tell me—which kills faster,

271
00:20:10,310 --> 00:20:11,880
a bullet or a string?

272
00:20:15,880 --> 00:20:16,750
If you ask me,

273
00:20:17,860 --> 00:20:20,060
killing is wrong no matter how you do it.

274
00:20:20,310 --> 00:20:22,110
Even killing traitors is wrong?

275
00:20:33,720 --> 00:20:35,180
Even Yeller knows that...

276
00:20:36,740 --> 00:20:37,930
the NBIS's Hurricane Team

277
00:20:37,930 --> 00:20:41,790
is in Shanghai carrying out
Mr. Dai's mission to eliminate traitors.

278
00:20:48,400 --> 00:20:49,710
I'm just a blind man.

279
00:20:52,920 --> 00:20:53,750
Chen Kailai!

280
00:20:54,070 --> 00:20:54,960
Chen Kailai!

281
00:20:56,510 --> 00:20:57,510
Chen Kailai!

282
00:20:58,030 --> 00:20:58,960
Chen Kailai!

283
00:20:58,980 --> 00:20:59,740
I'm here.

284
00:21:01,720 --> 00:21:02,480
Let me see.

285
00:21:03,050 --> 00:21:03,860
You're hurt.

286
00:21:03,890 --> 00:21:05,450
No, no, easy. Be gentle.

287
00:21:05,550 --> 00:21:06,810
I lost my fingernails.

288
00:21:07,680 --> 00:21:08,940
Then sit down quickly.

289
00:21:09,590 --> 00:21:11,320
Your whole face is injured too.

290
00:21:13,200 --> 00:21:14,470
I was so worried about you.

291
00:21:14,470 --> 00:21:15,920
Getting out of No. 76—

292
00:21:15,940 --> 00:21:18,550
that's practically like
returning to the land of the living.

293
00:21:18,550 --> 00:21:19,920
I didn't kill the man.

294
00:21:20,070 --> 00:21:21,730
Why wouldn't they release me?

295
00:21:21,790 --> 00:21:22,840
Those bastards

296
00:21:23,110 --> 00:21:24,920
don't need evidence to arrest people.

297
00:21:24,920 --> 00:21:26,260
If I hadn't pulled some strings,

298
00:21:26,260 --> 00:21:27,720
you'd have lost your life.

299
00:21:27,750 --> 00:21:28,950
Pulled some strings?

300
00:21:30,880 --> 00:21:32,680
This is my sworn sister, Shasha—

301
00:21:32,720 --> 00:21:34,660
our bond runs deeper than the sea
and is stronger

302
00:21:34,660 --> 00:21:35,340
than gold.

303
00:21:36,680 --> 00:21:38,140
Jinbao's a real sucker for love.

304
00:21:38,140 --> 00:21:39,510
I'd never spend 5,000 yuan

305
00:21:39,510 --> 00:21:40,680
on any man.

306
00:21:41,590 --> 00:21:42,200
How much?

307
00:21:42,350 --> 00:21:44,550
Five thousand. You have to give me an IOU.

308
00:21:44,550 --> 00:21:45,480
Five thousand?

309
00:21:45,810 --> 00:21:46,610
Are you crazy?

310
00:21:47,070 --> 00:21:49,130
Who asked you to pay people off for me?

311
00:21:49,160 --> 00:21:50,180
Weren't you broke?

312
00:21:50,180 --> 00:21:51,440
Where did you get the 5,000?

313
00:21:51,440 --> 00:21:52,330
Young Master Feng gave it to me.

314
00:21:52,330 --> 00:21:53,740
I put my name on an IOU for this money.

315
00:21:53,740 --> 00:21:55,000
You're paying it back.

316
00:21:55,960 --> 00:21:58,020
H-How am I supposed to pay back 5,000?

317
00:21:58,240 --> 00:21:59,510
They already agreed to let me go.

318
00:21:59,510 --> 00:22:00,970
Why did you have to butt in?

319
00:22:01,860 --> 00:22:03,610
I helped you, and now I'm in the wrong?

320
00:22:03,610 --> 00:22:04,640
All this misery, just because

321
00:22:04,640 --> 00:22:05,740
I ate one bowl of your wontons.

322
00:22:05,740 --> 00:22:06,500
Exactly.

323
00:22:06,680 --> 00:22:08,030
Jinbao, this lover of yours

324
00:22:08,030 --> 00:22:09,960
is nothing compared to my Cang.

325
00:22:10,150 --> 00:22:11,390
I'm not her lover.

326
00:22:11,570 --> 00:22:12,550
I'm her photographer.

327
00:22:12,550 --> 00:22:13,550
If you're not her lover,

328
00:22:13,550 --> 00:22:15,400
then why did Jinbao
go to all that trouble to save you?

329
00:22:15,400 --> 00:22:16,830
Men are all heartless.

330
00:22:16,860 --> 00:22:17,500
Agreed.

331
00:22:21,200 --> 00:22:22,200
Five thousand...

332
00:22:23,240 --> 00:22:24,170
Dinner's ready!

333
00:22:28,200 --> 00:22:29,260
Alright, alright.

334
00:22:29,310 --> 00:22:30,400
Let's go eat first.

335
00:22:30,400 --> 00:22:31,720
How am I supposed to eat?

336
00:22:31,720 --> 00:22:32,680
It's 5,000 yuan.

337
00:22:32,680 --> 00:22:34,000
How can I swallow anything after that?

338
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:35,920
Six for luck! Five for top honors!

339
00:22:35,920 --> 00:22:36,680
Drink!

340
00:22:41,110 --> 00:22:41,790
Kailai,

341
00:22:42,830 --> 00:22:46,400
another toast—
may your youthful ambition never fade,

342
00:22:46,720 --> 00:22:49,980
and may you conquer all enemies
like a general from heaven.

343
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:51,530
That sounds pretty heroic.

344
00:22:53,350 --> 00:22:53,980
Come on.

345
00:22:59,710 --> 00:23:00,920
Slow down.

346
00:23:01,880 --> 00:23:03,880
That damn Cang Guanglian,

347
00:23:04,110 --> 00:23:06,640
he promised to take care of my parents.

348
00:23:06,770 --> 00:23:08,340
That's why I became his.

349
00:23:11,590 --> 00:23:12,790
You promised me too.

350
00:23:13,920 --> 00:23:15,130
What did I promise you?

351
00:23:15,130 --> 00:23:16,790
You promised to pay back the money.

352
00:23:16,790 --> 00:23:18,750
If you can't, you'll have to marry me.

353
00:23:18,750 --> 00:23:19,750
Nonsense.

354
00:23:20,400 --> 00:23:21,160
Chen Kailai,

355
00:23:21,440 --> 00:23:22,950
you should have some conscience.

356
00:23:22,950 --> 00:23:23,870
I can testify.

357
00:23:25,150 --> 00:23:25,800
Come on, come on.

358
00:23:25,800 --> 00:23:26,930
Let's raise a glass.

359
00:23:27,510 --> 00:23:29,440
To Kailai for surviving an ordeal.

360
00:23:29,550 --> 00:23:30,480
Come on, come on.

361
00:23:30,720 --> 00:23:31,850
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

362
00:23:31,880 --> 00:23:33,080
To survive an ordeal.

363
00:23:44,570 --> 00:23:47,410
[Fulai Photo Studio]

364
00:24:05,550 --> 00:24:06,480
Master...

365
00:24:10,310 --> 00:24:11,350
What "Master"?

366
00:24:15,120 --> 00:24:16,230
You're drunk.

367
00:24:34,440 --> 00:24:35,500
The guy named Yu...

368
00:24:37,030 --> 00:24:38,200
you killed him.

369
00:24:39,440 --> 00:24:40,270
That certain?

370
00:24:52,270 --> 00:24:54,930
You wouldn't have suffered
if you'd given me up.

371
00:24:56,270 --> 00:24:57,400
Why didn't you?

372
00:25:03,030 --> 00:25:04,480
Because in Nanjing,

373
00:25:05,790 --> 00:25:08,450
you protected the common people
with your life.

374
00:25:12,510 --> 00:25:13,910
And you protected me too.

375
00:25:27,120 --> 00:25:29,010
Here you go. Your wontons.

376
00:25:29,830 --> 00:25:30,550
Enjoy.

377
00:25:31,440 --> 00:25:32,030
Sir,

378
00:25:32,640 --> 00:25:35,170
why is the Chunguang Photo Studio
sealed off?

379
00:25:37,920 --> 00:25:39,070
The Japanese did it.

380
00:25:39,280 --> 00:25:40,330
I heard the owner

381
00:25:40,810 --> 00:25:41,920
is a Communist.

382
00:25:42,420 --> 00:25:44,350
[Uncle Hai,
Underground Communist Party Member]

383
00:25:43,550 --> 00:25:44,480
Then where is he?

384
00:25:44,520 --> 00:25:45,270
Dead.

385
00:25:45,380 --> 00:25:46,440
He died on the spot.

386
00:25:46,790 --> 00:25:47,830
You didn't see it—

387
00:25:48,590 --> 00:25:49,520
it was so tragic.

388
00:25:51,070 --> 00:25:52,400
Please enjoy your meal.

389
00:26:19,350 --> 00:26:20,950
Broken Bridge gave his life.

390
00:26:37,000 --> 00:26:38,800
Then who exactly is Chen Kailai?

391
00:26:39,680 --> 00:26:41,740
He's just an ordinary photographer.

392
00:27:01,020 --> 00:27:02,500
Are you... Inspector Su?

393
00:27:04,550 --> 00:27:06,720
I'm Jin Meina
from the Telecommunications Section.

394
00:27:06,720 --> 00:27:08,030
Director Li is occupied with
official business,

395
00:27:08,030 --> 00:27:09,490
so he asked me to see to you.

396
00:27:43,310 --> 00:27:44,720
What a dump.

397
00:27:45,830 --> 00:27:47,110
They did it on purpose.

398
00:27:48,030 --> 00:27:49,920
At least we've made it into No. 76.

399
00:27:54,000 --> 00:27:56,460
When will Hoshino Eisei arrive
in Shanghai?

400
00:27:58,310 --> 00:27:59,710
Day after tomorrow, 8 AM.

401
00:28:06,110 --> 00:28:08,240
The Japanese want to end the war early.

402
00:28:09,960 --> 00:28:11,960
Project Slumber is their last hope.

403
00:28:13,310 --> 00:28:14,590
Dr. Hoshino

404
00:28:15,100 --> 00:28:16,290
is their trump card.

405
00:28:26,590 --> 00:28:28,240
He can be our trump card too.

406
00:28:39,000 --> 00:28:41,130
Next, we need to be more high-profile.

407
00:28:41,400 --> 00:28:43,270
We need to make sure all of Shanghai

408
00:28:43,270 --> 00:28:44,110
sees it.

409
00:29:01,680 --> 00:29:04,880
That night, you called me "Master."

410
00:29:06,350 --> 00:29:07,610
I called you "Master"?

411
00:29:08,350 --> 00:29:10,070
You need a master

412
00:29:10,680 --> 00:29:14,210
to teach you how to survive
and establish yourself in Shanghai.

413
00:29:14,750 --> 00:29:16,200
I know how to take photos.

414
00:29:16,590 --> 00:29:17,920
That's my skill.

415
00:29:18,440 --> 00:29:19,960
In these turbulent times,

416
00:29:19,990 --> 00:29:21,750
can a camera keep you alive?

417
00:29:23,510 --> 00:29:25,680
There's still a lot you need to learn.

418
00:29:25,680 --> 00:29:26,440
From now on,

419
00:29:26,790 --> 00:29:29,240
come to the bathhouse more often
and take a bath.

420
00:29:29,240 --> 00:29:30,440
Again with the baths?

421
00:29:31,440 --> 00:29:33,310
I almost lost my life last time.

422
00:29:33,400 --> 00:29:34,960
As long as you listen to me,

423
00:29:35,680 --> 00:29:37,310
you'll stay alive.

424
00:29:40,350 --> 00:29:41,810
You don't intend to remain

425
00:29:41,920 --> 00:29:44,110
just a photographer forever, do you?

426
00:30:02,270 --> 00:30:03,000
Chen Kailai.

427
00:30:15,880 --> 00:30:17,280
Do you still remember me?

428
00:30:19,110 --> 00:30:19,720
I do.

429
00:30:30,710 --> 00:30:32,440
Where is that pretty lady boss?

430
00:30:32,720 --> 00:30:33,650
You mean Jinbao?

431
00:30:34,070 --> 00:30:35,160
She just went out.

432
00:30:35,550 --> 00:30:37,280
Usually, I mind the shop alone.

433
00:30:40,750 --> 00:30:43,270
What made you come all the way to Shanghai
to open a studio?

434
00:30:43,270 --> 00:30:44,510
My master sent me.

435
00:30:49,680 --> 00:30:51,140
Then where is your master?

436
00:30:51,640 --> 00:30:52,440
He died.

437
00:30:56,510 --> 00:30:57,640
Right in front of me.

438
00:31:00,070 --> 00:31:01,070
I came to Shanghai

439
00:31:02,000 --> 00:31:03,240
just to finish

440
00:31:03,750 --> 00:31:05,280
what he never got to finish.

441
00:31:06,000 --> 00:31:07,330
Opening a photo studio?

442
00:31:08,960 --> 00:31:11,420
And waiting for the person
he wanted to meet.

443
00:31:14,480 --> 00:31:15,510
Did you meet them?

444
00:31:20,000 --> 00:31:22,310
I forgot the secret code last time.

445
00:31:25,000 --> 00:31:25,880
What code?

446
00:31:32,790 --> 00:31:33,510
She said,

447
00:31:34,640 --> 00:31:37,040
"Your camera is American-made, isn't it?"

448
00:31:37,480 --> 00:31:38,200
I said,

449
00:31:38,960 --> 00:31:40,560
"My camera is German-made."

450
00:31:43,240 --> 00:31:45,240
I heard there's color film now.

451
00:31:46,110 --> 00:31:46,720
Yes,

452
00:31:47,510 --> 00:31:49,750
but I still prefer black-and-white film.

453
00:31:49,750 --> 00:31:50,720
Black is black,

454
00:31:51,350 --> 00:31:52,410
and white is white.

455
00:31:56,160 --> 00:31:58,090
Then how could you forget the code?

456
00:31:59,030 --> 00:32:00,400
He died so suddenly

457
00:32:00,550 --> 00:32:01,610
and didn't tell me.

458
00:32:01,810 --> 00:32:03,260
I figured it out myself.

459
00:32:06,980 --> 00:32:08,920
You've thrown
the whole plan into disarray.

460
00:32:08,920 --> 00:32:11,050
The Organization will need to vet you.

461
00:32:12,610 --> 00:32:13,410
I understand.

462
00:32:18,960 --> 00:32:20,220
Hello, Broken Bridge.

463
00:32:20,960 --> 00:32:21,920
I'm Su Causeway.

464
00:32:29,350 --> 00:32:30,280
This is so great.

465
00:32:49,680 --> 00:32:52,030
These are what Li Musheng left behind.

466
00:32:52,030 --> 00:32:53,030
They're all here.

467
00:33:12,830 --> 00:33:14,350
Did he leave you any instructions?

468
00:33:14,350 --> 00:33:15,110
No.

469
00:33:15,830 --> 00:33:17,750
Everything happened so suddenly.

470
00:33:17,750 --> 00:33:20,080
I even had to guess
the secret code myself.

471
00:33:26,640 --> 00:33:27,790
Who is this woman?

472
00:33:28,400 --> 00:33:30,030
Why did Li Musheng copy all her letters

473
00:33:30,030 --> 00:33:31,200
into his notebook?

474
00:33:33,640 --> 00:33:34,550
You read them?

475
00:33:34,960 --> 00:33:36,310
I memorized every one.

476
00:33:39,070 --> 00:33:40,600
Then who do you think she is?

477
00:33:44,750 --> 00:33:45,640
A young woman

478
00:33:46,480 --> 00:33:47,340
from Shanghai.

479
00:33:48,350 --> 00:33:50,720
She lived in Tokyo for a while.

480
00:33:52,240 --> 00:33:54,680
She kept up correspondence with Li Musheng
the whole time,

481
00:33:54,680 --> 00:33:56,280
but they never actually met.

482
00:33:56,680 --> 00:33:58,880
She must've been a confidante of sorts.

483
00:34:01,680 --> 00:34:04,210
You figured all that out
from the letters too?

484
00:34:05,160 --> 00:34:07,220
He never mentioned this person to me.

485
00:34:10,670 --> 00:34:11,800
This was his secret.

486
00:34:14,510 --> 00:34:15,760
I was wondering why this old bachelor

487
00:34:15,760 --> 00:34:17,110
never got married.

488
00:34:17,840 --> 00:34:20,699
Turns out someone was
living in his heart all along.

489
00:34:22,030 --> 00:34:24,360
I always thought I knew him well.

490
00:34:25,030 --> 00:34:26,690
I even looked down on him a bit.

491
00:34:26,880 --> 00:34:27,810
I never imagined

492
00:34:28,000 --> 00:34:29,659
he was hiding so many secrets.

493
00:34:33,840 --> 00:34:35,070
How did you two meet?

494
00:34:36,230 --> 00:34:37,280
I met him in Nanjing

495
00:34:37,280 --> 00:34:39,230
when I was a war correspondent.

496
00:34:39,960 --> 00:34:41,960
He said he had a photo studio in Hangzhou

497
00:34:41,960 --> 00:34:42,760
and needed an assistant,

498
00:34:42,760 --> 00:34:43,670
so I went.

499
00:34:44,760 --> 00:34:46,889
Many of us went to Nanjing at that time.

500
00:34:47,670 --> 00:34:49,000
So your meeting

501
00:34:49,150 --> 00:34:50,550
wasn't really a coincidence.

502
00:34:50,550 --> 00:34:52,679
I always thought he was quite worldly.

503
00:34:53,230 --> 00:34:54,030
Turns out

504
00:34:54,320 --> 00:34:55,710
he was a Communist.

505
00:35:01,280 --> 00:35:02,540
Thank you for all this.

506
00:35:02,710 --> 00:35:04,360
You've been a great help to us.

507
00:35:04,360 --> 00:35:06,590
Is there anything else I can help with?

508
00:35:08,000 --> 00:35:08,710
No need.

509
00:35:09,320 --> 00:35:11,030
You've already done more than enough.

510
00:35:11,030 --> 00:35:11,960
This is it?

511
00:35:18,150 --> 00:35:18,880
Then...

512
00:35:19,320 --> 00:35:21,000
can I take a picture of you?

513
00:35:25,360 --> 00:35:26,000
Sure.

514
00:35:31,070 --> 00:35:32,840
What does this hold?

515
00:35:33,360 --> 00:35:35,110
All the beauty in the world.

516
00:35:35,400 --> 00:35:37,460
What is "all the beauty in the world"?

517
00:35:38,440 --> 00:35:39,570
I don't know either.

518
00:35:39,800 --> 00:35:41,510
Whatever it is, it's beautiful.

519
00:35:41,510 --> 00:35:43,440
But I'll definitely know someday.

520
00:35:44,670 --> 00:35:45,360
Ready?

521
00:35:45,710 --> 00:35:46,440
Look here.

522
00:35:48,440 --> 00:35:51,300
Do you still remember
what we said when we were kids?

523
00:35:53,030 --> 00:35:53,960
What is

524
00:35:54,480 --> 00:35:56,140
"all the beauty in the world"?

525
00:35:59,400 --> 00:36:00,480
Now I know.

526
00:36:02,670 --> 00:36:04,070
The most beautiful thing

527
00:36:04,880 --> 00:36:05,710
is peace.

528
00:36:10,070 --> 00:36:10,670
Look here.

529
00:36:26,000 --> 00:36:26,630
Will we...

530
00:36:27,480 --> 00:36:28,680
see each other again?

531
00:36:29,550 --> 00:36:30,280
I don't know.

532
00:36:31,440 --> 00:36:33,500
Then where can I find you if I need you?

533
00:36:34,300 --> 00:36:35,630
Just be a photographer.

534
00:36:42,800 --> 00:36:43,440
Goodbye.

535
00:37:16,320 --> 00:37:17,230
Inspector Su?

536
00:37:25,760 --> 00:37:26,690
What do you want?

537
00:37:27,280 --> 00:37:28,880
Get in. We'll talk in the car.

538
00:37:40,000 --> 00:37:40,960
How's business?

539
00:37:42,000 --> 00:37:42,710
Not so good.

540
00:37:44,480 --> 00:37:45,880
How about I find you a job?

541
00:37:46,400 --> 00:37:47,030
Sure.

542
00:37:49,400 --> 00:37:50,670
Be my photographer.

543
00:37:51,000 --> 00:37:51,670
No.

544
00:37:54,760 --> 00:37:56,480
There are plenty of photographers
in Shanghai—

545
00:37:56,480 --> 00:37:57,810
why does it have to be me?

546
00:37:58,530 --> 00:38:00,510
Because you make me look better in photos.

547
00:38:00,510 --> 00:38:01,970
Flattery won't work on me.

548
00:38:05,280 --> 00:38:06,670
Because I'm a traitor?

549
00:38:07,430 --> 00:38:08,760
You said that yourself.

550
00:38:10,530 --> 00:38:12,600
Are all you people at No. 76 like this?

551
00:38:13,030 --> 00:38:16,230
You ask me questions,
but you don't want to hear the truth.

552
00:38:25,970 --> 00:38:27,260
Why be a photographer?

553
00:38:28,150 --> 00:38:29,480
To make a living.

554
00:38:31,590 --> 00:38:32,190
That's it?

555
00:38:35,030 --> 00:38:37,320
And maybe take photos of things
that matter,

556
00:38:37,320 --> 00:38:38,400
to record this era.

557
00:38:41,480 --> 00:38:42,630
Taking photos of me

558
00:38:42,960 --> 00:38:45,960
is more meaningful
than working in a studio, isn't it?

559
00:38:45,960 --> 00:38:46,820
I don't see how.

560
00:38:50,630 --> 00:38:52,090
Just do it to make a living.

561
00:38:53,880 --> 00:38:54,920
I'm expensive.

562
00:38:57,230 --> 00:38:58,160
Name your price.

563
00:39:01,350 --> 00:39:02,390
Then...

564
00:39:03,150 --> 00:39:04,000
100 yuan a day?

565
00:39:04,000 --> 00:39:05,330
You've got a death wish?

566
00:39:05,360 --> 00:39:06,070
Deal.

567
00:39:08,960 --> 00:39:09,760
Are you sure?

568
00:39:12,000 --> 00:39:14,460
A car will come pick you up
tomorrow morning.

569
00:39:15,030 --> 00:39:16,550
I think that female pervert

570
00:39:16,550 --> 00:39:17,950
has taken a liking to you.

571
00:39:18,190 --> 00:39:19,110
How shameless.

572
00:39:19,760 --> 00:39:20,850
No way.

573
00:39:23,620 --> 00:39:24,660
Well,

574
00:39:25,030 --> 00:39:26,960
if only she weren't a traitor.

575
00:39:31,760 --> 00:39:33,150
You're even dreaming about her now?

576
00:39:33,150 --> 00:39:34,070
I'm telling you,

577
00:39:34,070 --> 00:39:35,000
if you dare to go,

578
00:39:35,000 --> 00:39:36,200
I'll break your legs.

579
00:39:37,070 --> 00:39:38,670
I don't want to go either.

580
00:39:39,110 --> 00:39:40,840
I just couldn't keep my mouth shut.

581
00:39:40,840 --> 00:39:43,100
I meant to scare her off
with a high price,

582
00:39:43,280 --> 00:39:44,400
but she agreed.

583
00:39:45,880 --> 00:39:47,280
Now you regret it?

584
00:39:47,670 --> 00:39:49,880
Here I am, the beautiful
dancing queen from Hangzhou—

585
00:39:49,880 --> 00:39:50,880
you wouldn't photograph me

586
00:39:50,880 --> 00:39:52,840
but insist on
photographing that she-devil.

587
00:39:52,840 --> 00:39:54,840
You think you've got lives to spare?

588
00:39:55,960 --> 00:39:58,110
That she-devil really is strange.

589
00:39:59,150 --> 00:40:00,440
You could say she's good,

590
00:40:00,440 --> 00:40:01,570
but she's a traitor.

591
00:40:01,920 --> 00:40:03,190
You could say she's bad,

592
00:40:03,190 --> 00:40:04,390
yet she saved my life.

593
00:40:05,190 --> 00:40:07,320
You didn't kill him in the first place.

594
00:40:07,760 --> 00:40:08,550
At most,

595
00:40:08,550 --> 00:40:10,480
she's got a bit of conscience left.

596
00:40:11,030 --> 00:40:12,920
Then why do you think
she specifically wants me

597
00:40:12,920 --> 00:40:14,320
to take her photographs?

598
00:40:15,590 --> 00:40:17,710
You just said you named a high price?

599
00:40:20,280 --> 00:40:21,480
How much did you name?

600
00:40:21,840 --> 00:40:23,030
More than you pay me.

601
00:40:23,880 --> 00:40:24,680
How much more?

602
00:40:28,710 --> 00:40:29,510
Ten yuan?

603
00:40:30,430 --> 00:40:31,780
One hundred yuan a day.

604
00:40:35,030 --> 00:40:35,920
Really?

605
00:40:36,480 --> 00:40:37,280
Are you sure

606
00:40:37,780 --> 00:40:39,580
she just wants you to take photos

607
00:40:39,590 --> 00:40:40,670
and nothing else?

608
00:40:42,360 --> 00:40:43,620
What are you thinking?

609
00:40:44,070 --> 00:40:45,200
Just taking photos.

610
00:40:45,880 --> 00:40:46,320
Go.

611
00:40:46,670 --> 00:40:47,800
You have to go.

612
00:40:48,400 --> 00:40:49,590
Even if you have to do something else,

613
00:40:49,590 --> 00:40:50,720
you still have to go.

614
00:40:51,190 --> 00:40:53,390
Now you don't mind that she's a traitor?

615
00:40:53,960 --> 00:40:54,760
She is.

616
00:40:54,800 --> 00:40:56,600
As long as you're not, it's fine.

617
00:40:56,860 --> 00:40:58,260
Come on, do the math.

618
00:40:59,030 --> 00:41:00,030
One hundred each time,

619
00:41:00,030 --> 00:41:01,690
and ten times is one thousand.

620
00:41:02,190 --> 00:41:04,590
You sure changed your tune pretty quickly.

621
00:41:04,840 --> 00:41:06,190
Have you forgotten how you cursed her out

622
00:41:06,190 --> 00:41:07,840
last time when you were drunk?

623
00:41:07,840 --> 00:41:09,570
A person has to keep their word.

624
00:41:09,760 --> 00:41:10,890
Once we name a price,

625
00:41:11,000 --> 00:41:12,400
we have to honor the deal.

626
00:41:12,630 --> 00:41:14,720
That's the basic principle
of doing business.

627
00:41:14,720 --> 00:41:15,440
Besides,

628
00:41:15,920 --> 00:41:17,110
if you back out now,

629
00:41:17,550 --> 00:41:19,630
do you think
that she-devil will let you off?

630
00:41:19,630 --> 00:41:22,670
What if she has you thrown back in there
to suffer again?

631
00:41:22,670 --> 00:41:24,510
The wound on your hand just healed—

632
00:41:24,510 --> 00:41:26,170
imagine how much that'd hurt.

633
00:41:27,030 --> 00:41:28,070
Money-grubber.

634
00:41:29,050 --> 00:41:29,880
Such a miser.

635
00:41:29,960 --> 00:41:31,490
Can you live without money?

636
00:41:32,150 --> 00:41:34,550
Still, we shouldn't
just care about money.

637
00:41:34,630 --> 00:41:37,440
This country needs
people with conviction to save it.

638
00:41:37,440 --> 00:41:38,280
You?

639
00:41:38,550 --> 00:41:40,480
Save the photo studio first, okay?

640
00:41:40,670 --> 00:41:42,400
You're hardly the one to save the country.

641
00:41:42,400 --> 00:41:43,760
I can't get through to you.

642
00:41:43,760 --> 00:41:44,710
Chen Kailai!

643
00:41:45,230 --> 00:41:46,890
You need to have a conscience!

644
00:41:47,280 --> 00:41:48,230
To save you,

645
00:41:48,230 --> 00:41:50,310
I borrowed money from Young Master Feng.

646
00:41:50,310 --> 00:41:51,570
Young Master Feng said

647
00:41:51,840 --> 00:41:52,900
if I don't pay him back,

648
00:41:52,900 --> 00:41:54,510
I'll have to marry into his family!

649
00:41:54,510 --> 00:41:55,640
That's a good thing.

650
00:41:55,890 --> 00:41:57,620
Young Master Feng is a good guy.

651
00:41:57,760 --> 00:41:58,760
Not marrying him!

652
00:41:59,030 --> 00:42:00,230
Marrying his father.

653
00:42:00,510 --> 00:42:01,510
He's already 80.

654
00:42:02,920 --> 00:42:03,710
Eighty?

655
00:42:04,280 --> 00:42:05,280
How's his health?

656
00:42:06,360 --> 00:42:07,490
Not good, of course.

657
00:42:08,230 --> 00:42:10,160
Then he doesn't have many years left.

658
00:42:10,160 --> 00:42:10,880
I think it's a good match.

659
00:42:10,880 --> 00:42:12,190
Just grit your teeth and get through it.

660
00:42:12,190 --> 00:42:13,650
Chen Kailai, you bastard!

661
00:42:13,970 --> 00:42:15,800
I haven't forgotten the money I owe you.

662
00:42:15,800 --> 00:42:17,010
What good does remembering it do?

663
00:42:17,010 --> 00:42:17,880
You have to pay it back!

664
00:42:17,880 --> 00:42:19,340
I will! I definitely will!

665
00:42:22,940 --> 00:42:26,110
[Hoshino, Japanese Medical Doctor]

666
00:42:37,420 --> 00:42:38,050
Ishida.

667
00:42:42,230 --> 00:42:43,430
It's been a long time.

668
00:42:44,160 --> 00:42:45,590
[Ishida,
Japanese Bacteriology Lab Technician]

669
00:42:48,440 --> 00:42:49,840
It's been a long journey.

670
00:42:50,390 --> 00:42:51,590
Welcome to Shanghai.

671
00:42:57,110 --> 00:42:57,880
Look here.

672
00:42:58,960 --> 00:42:59,800
Smile.

673
00:43:00,110 --> 00:43:01,550
Three, two...
